ype":"h","text":"Year 2 — Networking & Transmission"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student should begin moving from general electronics toward telecommunications."},{"type":"h","text":"Networking Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OSI model"},{"text":"TCP/IP model"},{"text":"Ethernet"},{"text":"MAC addresses"},{"text":"IP addressing"},{"text":"IPv4"},{"text":"IPv6"},{"text":"Subnetting"},{"text":"ARP"},{"text":"DNS"},{"text":"DHCP"},{"text":"NAT"},{"text":"Routing"},{"text":"Switching"},{"text":"VLAN basics"},{"text":"TCP/UDP"},{"text":"HTTP/HTTPS"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Device","Access Network","Aggregation","Transport Network","Core Network","Internet / Service Network"]},{"type":"h","text":"Fiber-Optic Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Fiber is an especially valuable skill for telecom field roles."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Optical fiber fundamentals"},{"text":"Single-mode fiber"},{"text":"Multimode fiber"},{"text":"Fiber connectors"},{"text":"Fiber splicing"},{"text":"Optical attenuation"},{"text":"Optical power"},{"text":"Fiber loss"},{"text":"OTDR concepts"},{"text":"Optical transmitters"},{"text":"Optical receivers"},{"text":"OLT/ONU concepts"},{"text":"FTTH architecture"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Equipment"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the use of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Optical Power Meter"},{"text":"OTDR"},{"text":"Visual Fault Locator"},{"text":"Fusion Splicer"},{"text":"Fiber Cleaver"},{"text":"Fiber Inspection tools"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A technician should understand the complete workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Fiber Installation","Connector / Splice","Optical Power Test","OTDR Test","Loss Analysis","Fault Identification","Repair","Final Verification"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Wireless, RF & Mobile Networks"},{"type":"h","text":"RF Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frequency spectrum"},{"text":"Wavelength"},{"text":"Amplitude"},{"text":"Phase"},{"text":"Gain"},{"text":"Loss"},{"text":"dB/dBm"},{"text":"Antenna gain"},{"text":"Propagation"},{"text":"Reflection"},{"text":"Refraction"},{"text":"Diffraction"},{"text":"Multipath"},{"text":"Interference"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RF cables"},{"text":"Connectors"},{"text":"Antennas"},{"text":"Feeders"},{"text":"RF power"},{"text":"Signal strength"},{"text":"Coverage"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mobile Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop conceptual understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"2G"},{"text":"3G"},{"text":"4G LTE"},{"text":"5G"},{"text":"SIM/eSIM"},{"text":"Cell sites"},{"text":"Base stations"},{"text":"Small cells"},{"text":"Backhaul"},{"text":"Radio Access Network (RAN)"},{"text":"Core network"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For 4G/5G, understand the broad architecture:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mobile Device","Radio Access Network","Transport / Backhaul","Core Network","Internet / Applications"]},{"type":"p","text":"The technician does not necessarily need to become a telecom network architect, but should understand how these components interact."},{"type":"h","text":"Telecom Equipment"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Access Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ONT/ONU"},{"text":"OLT"},{"text":"DSL equipment"},{"text":"Broadband routers"},{"text":"Access switches"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Transmission Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Optical transmission systems"},{"text":"Microwave links"},{"text":"Fiber links"},{"text":"Multiplexers"},{"text":"Transport equipment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Wireless Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radio units"},{"text":"Antennas"},{"text":"Baseband equipment"},{"text":"RF modules"},{"text":"Small-cell equipment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Supporting Systems"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Telecom power supplies"},{"text":"Rectifiers"},{"text":"Batteries"},{"text":"UPS"},{"text":"Grounding"},{"text":"Surge protection"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4 — Telecom Troubleshooting"},{"type":"p","text":"Troubleshooting should become one of the strongest skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Fault-Diagnosis Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Customer / Network Problem","Collect Symptoms","Check Power","Check Physical Connections","Check Link Status","Measure Signal","Check Configuration","Isolate Fault","Repair / Replace","Retest","Document Resolution"]},{"type":"h","text":"Common Faults to Understand"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fiber cuts"},{"text":"High optical loss"},{"text":"Loose connectors"},{"text":"Faulty SFP modules"},{"text":"Damaged cables"},{"text":"Power failures"},{"text":"Network link failures"},{"text":"RF interference"},{"text":"Poor signal strength"},{"text":"Configuration errors"},{"text":"Faulty routers/switches"},{"text":"Antenna/feedline problems"},{"text":"Transmission link failures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Network Troubleshooting Tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn practical use of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ping"},{"text":"traceroute/tracert"},{"text":"ipconfig/ifconfig"},{"text":"nslookup"},{"text":"arp"},{"text":"netstat"},{"text":"curl"},{"text":"Wireshark"},{"text":"Basic Linux networking commands"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how to interpret:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Packet loss"},{"text":"Latency"},{"text":"Jitter"},{"text":"Throughput"},{"text":"Interface errors"},{"text":"Link status"},{"text":"Signal levels"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project Ideas"}]},{"heading":"FTTH Network Design & Monitoring System","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Create a simulated or small-scale FTTH architecture."},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OLT"},{"text":"Optical distribution"},{"text":"ONT"},{"text":"Fiber links"},{"text":"Optical power analysis"},{"text":"Network monitoring"}]}]},{"heading":"Fiber-Optic Fault Detection System","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop a system or analytical model for identifying:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fiber cuts"},{"text":"Excessive attenuation"},{"text":"Connector problems"},{"text":"Abnormal optical loss"},{"text":"Document the test methodology and limitations."}]}]},{"heading":"IoT-Based Telecom Equipment Monitoring","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Monitor:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equipment temperature"},{"text":"Power supply"},{"text":"Battery voltage"},{"text":"Environmental conditions"},{"text":"Equipment status"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"flow","items":["ESP32","sensors","communication","dashboard"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Network Performance Monitoring System","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop a small monitoring platform measuring:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Latency"},{"text":"Packet loss"},{"text":"Availability"},{"text":"Bandwidth"},{"text":"Device status"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible stack:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Python","SNMP concepts","database","dashboard"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Wireless Signal Measurement & Coverage Study","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a practical study of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Signal strength"},{"text":"Coverage"},{"text":"Interference"},{"text":"Indoor/outdoor propagation"},{"text":"Distance vs signal quality"},{"text":"Present results using maps and graphs."}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize internships where you get actual field or laboratory exposure."},{"type":"h","text":"Telecom Operators"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore internships or training involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Network operations"},{"text":"Fiber deployment"},{"text":"Mobile networks"},{"text":"Transmission"},{"text":"Field maintenance"},{"text":"Network monitoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"ISP / Broadband Companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FTTH"},{"text":"Fiber installation"},{"text":"ONT/ONU"},{"text":"Routers"},{"text":"Access networks"},{"text":"Customer-premises troubleshooting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Telecom Infrastructure Companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Towers"},{"text":"Fiber"},{"text":"RF equipment"},{"text":"Power systems"},{"text":"Site maintenance"},{"text":"Transmission"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Network Equipment Companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hardware testing"},{"text":"Network testing"},{"text":"Equipment configuration"},{"text":"Technical support"},{"text":"Network operations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Electronics","Telecom / Networking Intern","Fiber / Field Technician Intern","Telecom Technician Trainee","Telecom Technician","Senior Telecom Technician"]},{"type":"p","text":"A field internship involving fiber testing, equipment installation, network troubleshooting or RF measurements is particularly valuable."}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A graduate can target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Telecom Technician"},{"text":"Junior Telecom Technician"},{"text":"Telecom Field Technician"},{"text":"Network Technician"},{"text":"Fiber Optic Technician"},{"text":"Fiber Technician"},{"text":"FTTH Technician"},{"text":"Broadband Technician"},{"text":"Transmission Technician"},{"text":"Telecom Maintenance Technician"},{"text":"Telecom Installation Technician"},{"text":"Telecom Test Technician"},{"text":"RF Technician"},{"text":"RF Field Technician"},{"text":"Wireless Technician"},{"text":"Network Support Technician"},{"text":"Network Operations Technician"},{"text":"NOC Technician"},{"text":"Telecom Equipment Technician"},{"text":"Field Service Technician"},{"text":"Optical Network Technician"},{"text":"Fiber Splicing Technicia